// Niri output configuration.
//
// Without explicit positions niri auto-places outputs in connector order,
// which put DP-1 at x=0 and HDMI-A-1 at x=1920 — the reverse of how they sit
// on the desk, so moving left/right landed on the wrong screen.
//
// Arrangement (arch-desktop): AOC on the LEFT, Dell on the RIGHT.
//
//     x=0            x=1600         x=3520
//     +--------------+--------------+
//     | HDMI-A-1     | DP-1         |
//     | AOC 1600x900 | Dell 1920x1080
//
// Only position is pinned; mode and scale stay on niri's preferred defaults
// (1600x900@60 and 1920x1080@60 respectively), so a monitor swap degrades
// gracefully instead of failing to find a hardcoded mode.
//
// Both are top-aligned (y=0). If the pointer catching on the height
// difference is annoying, bottom-align the shorter one with y=180
// (1080 - 900). Run `niri msg outputs` for connector names and geometry.
//
// To try a different arrangement without editing this file — takes effect
// instantly, forgotten on the next config reload:
//     niri msg output HDMI-A-1 position set 0 0
//     niri msg output DP-1 position set 1600 0

output "HDMI-A-1" {
    position x=0 y=0
}

output "DP-1" {
    position x=1600 y=0
}
